rine on which this city is named. It\'s located at the joining of the two sacred rivers of Gomti and Saryu. This shrine is devoted to Lord Shiva and is the place where he meditated in Bageshwar. It was constructed in 1450 by Laxmi Chand, a Kumaon King. The best time to visit this temple is during the Hindu jubilee of Shivratri when a joyful festivity is organized then drawing excursionists from all around India.</p><h3>Chandika Temple</h3><p>Chandika Temple is the holy shrine devoted to the Hindu deity Chandika Mai also referred to as Maa Kali. It is merely a half-kilometer from Bageshwar and attracts tourists, especially during the months of Navrataras. Further, Goddess Chandika Mai is a revered deity for the locals here and thus is a must-place to visit in Bageshwar and experience the divine tranquility this place possesses.</p><h3>Baijnath</h3><p>Located at a distance of 26 km from Bageshwar, Baijnath is an important place of interest, known for its early sanctuaries and named after the famous Baijnath temple then situated. Baijnath actually served as the capital during the time of the Katyuri lords during the 7th to 11th-century annals and its earlier name was Kartikeyapura located in the Katyur valley. The Baijnath temple was also built by the Katyuri kings enlarging the icons of Lord Shiva, Goddess Parvati, Lord Ganesha, Lord Brahma, and colorful other Hindu deities. Also, it is primarily dedicated to Lord Shiva, and as per Hindu mythology, it is said that the marriage of Lord Shiva and Goddess Parvati took place at the river Gomti and Garur Ganges.</p><p><br></p>','page',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Car Rental In Bageshwar: Cabs in Bageshwar Rs.9km only','Duracabs offerCar Rental In Bageshwar service 24x7. you book cabs in Bageshwar online for local and out stations trip from Bageshwar at very lowest prices.',NULL,'cab service in bagheshwar,taxi service,taxi service in bagheshwar,cab service,taxi service near me,car rental agencies in bagheshwar,one way cab taxi