even wonders of the world which is visited by a lot of tourist from different corners of world. Apart from the Taj Mahal, Agra is also known for other Mughal-era monuments like the Agra Fort , Sikandra fort and Fatehpur Sikri. Agra is also known for its rich cultural heritage, including handicrafts, dance, and its delicious cuisine, which features a mix of Mughlai and regional dishes. Also you will get to know a lot of delicious Street foods available in the local markets and streets of Agra.</p><h2>Places to Visit in Agra with Private Cab</h2><p>Agra is home to a lot of historical monuments which were built by Mughal emperors 100 of years back. Here are some of the most popular tourist attractions in Agra that you can visit:</p><p><strong><br>Taj Mahal<br>&nbsp;<br></strong><br></p><p>One of the Seven Wonders of the World, the Taj Mahal is built by Mughal emperor Shah Jahan in memory of his wife Mumtaz Mahal. It is a beautiful white marble monument that attracts millions of tourists from all over the world. Being in the list of seven wonders of the world it is heavily crowded by tourist all over the year.</p><p><strong><br>Agra Fort<br>&nbsp;<br></strong><br></p><p>Apart from Taj Mahal there are other thoughts and monuments that are visited by a lot of tourist. the Agra Fort is a popular tourist attraction and attracts visitors from around the world who come to admire its impressive architecture and rich history.</p><p><strong><br>Tomb of Akbar<br>&nbsp;<br></strong><br></p><p>The tomb is built in a large garden and is made of red sandstone and marble. It has four ornamental gates, each of which is decorated with stone carvings and calligraphy. The Tomb of Akbar is a popular tourist attraction and is visited by thousands of people every year who come to see the architecture of the monument and admire the beauty of the monument.</p><p><strong><br>Itmad-ud-daula<br>&nbsp;<br></strong><br></p><p>Itmad-ud-Daula is a Mughal monument located in Agra. It is also known as 