ttractions in Agra that you can visit:</p><p><br>Taj Mahal<br><br></p><p><br></p><p>One of the Seven Wonders of the World, the Taj Mahal is built by Mughal emperor Shah Jahan in memory of his wife, Mumtaz Mahal. It is a beautiful white marble monument that attracts millions of tourists from all over the world. Being in the list of seven wonders of the world, it is heavily crowded by tourists all year long.</p><p><br>Agra Fort<br><br></p><p><br></p><p>Apart from Taj Mahal, there are other forts and monuments that are visited by a lot of tourists. The Agra Fort is a popular tourist attraction and attracts visitors from around the world who come to admire its impressive architecture and rich history.</p><p><br>Tomb of Akbar<br><br></p><p><br></p><p>The tomb is built in a large garden and is made of red sandstone and marble. It has four ornamental gates, each of which is decorated with stone carvings and calligraphy. The Tomb of Akbar is a popular tourist attraction and is visited by thousands of people every year who come to see the architecture of the monument and admire the beauty of the monument.</p><p><br>Itmad-ud-daula<br><br></p><p><br></p><p>Itmad-ud-Daula is a Mughal monument located in Agra. It is also known as the \"Baby Taj\" because of its great resemblance to the Taj Mahal, which was built later. This is also made up of white marble but is a bit smaller than Taj Mahal. It is has a Persian-style garden with water channels, fountains, and fruit trees. The monument also has a mosque and a small museum.</p><p><br>Sikandra Fort<br><br></p><p><br></p><p>The Sikandra Fort is another historic fort located in Sikandra, Agra. It was built by Emperor Akbar and is a must-visit attraction for historians. People come here to admire the architecture and history of the Mughal times.</p><p><br>Fatehpur sikri<br><br></p><p><br></p><p>Fatehpur Sikri is a historical city located in Agra. It has many monuments, which are visited by many visitors. The city is surrounded by a fo